me Design – Connecticut\n\nTerracon supported a Connecticut ISP in the design and permitting \nof a fiber-to-the-home network serving approximately 3,500 subscribers.\n\nTerracon performed aerial make ready engineering, underground utility \nconflict analysis, and CAD drawing production for multiple municipalities, \nincluding coordination of 35 permit packages for submission to the \nstate DOT.\n\nFiber-to-the-Home Design – Connecticut case study specifics:\n• Aerial make ready engineering\n• Underground utility conflict analysis\n• CAD drawing production\n• 35 permit packages to state DOT\n• 3,500 subscribers\n\nFiber-to-the-Home Design – Large ISP\n\nTerracon is supporting one of the nation's largest broadband providers \nin the design and permitting of a residential fiber network.\n\nTerracon coordinated with nearly 200 municipalities for permit \nsubmissions, including coordination with state DOTs, counties, and \nmunicipal bodies across 4 states.\n\nFiber-to-the-Home Design – Large ISP case study specifics:\n• 200 municipalities\n• 4 states\n• State DOTs, counties, municipal bodies\n• Residential fiber network\n\n\nCurbside Fiber to the Home\n\nOne of the nation's top broadband providers engaged Terracon to \ndesign and permit a curbside fiber-to-the-home network.\n\nIn close collaboration with the client, Terracon developed customized \ndrawing templates in coordination with the client's GIS team. \n\nTerracon developed new systems and processes specifically for this \nwork, incorporating quality control, metadata, and standardization to \nproduce construction drawings and permit packages.\n\nTerracon's CAD team managed iterative drawing reviews, utilizing \nversioning and revision tracking, to bring permit submissions to \napproval-ready status quickly.\n\nCurbside Fiber to the Home case study specifics:\n• Customized drawing templates in coordination with client's GIS team\n• New systems and processes for QC, metadata, and standardization\n• Construction drawings and permit packages\n• CAD team managed iterative drawing reviews\n• Versioning and revision tracking\n• Approval-ready permit submissions\n\n\nDriving Broadband Infrastructure Programs at Scale\n\nTerracon supported a large broadband provider in the deployment of \na large-scale fiber-to-the-home network.\n\nTerracon's team coordinated with hundreds of municipalities, state \nagencies, and utility providers to secure permits and manage project \ncompliance.\n\nTerracon drove efficiencies across hundreds of permit applications in \nmultiple states by developing standardized processes, templates, and \nleveraging technology.\n\n\n"
